WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:05.839
Hi, guys. How are you? My name is Ilonka
and welcome to another video

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:07.966
on the Netflix channel.

00:00:11.886 --> 00:00:18.226
When we were kids, most families
only had an open TV at home.

00:00:18.268 --> 00:00:21.855
They had no cable channels,
like cartoons and those things.

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:25.150
And when they broadcasted
children's television,

00:00:25.275 --> 00:00:27.986
all the things we saw were anime.

00:00:28.111 --> 00:00:28.153
(When we were kids we all saw these anime)

00:00:28.153 --> 00:00:31.322
I came to school, when I was 6 years old,

00:00:31.406 --> 00:00:35.118
and everyone started talking
about the first episode of POKEMON.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:38.371
Everybody was watching it. I didn't know
what they were talking about.

00:00:38.496 --> 00:00:41.791
So I sat down and I began, diligently,

00:00:41.916 --> 00:00:44.753
diligently, diligently,

00:00:44.794 --> 00:00:46.671
to watch all POKEMON episodes.

00:00:46.796 --> 00:00:49.340
I became a happy girl
who could speak with everybody.

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:52.510
In fact, at recess, we played POKEMON.

00:00:52.594 --> 00:00:57.348
And we played to be coaches, and Pokémon,
and we had "Pokémon battles".

00:00:57.348 --> 00:00:58.892
All right. Quick attack.

00:00:58.975 --> 00:01:00.101
Chu!

00:01:00.185 --> 00:01:02.729
Raichu, take down now!

00:01:02.812 --> 00:01:06.149
-Rai!
-Pikachu!

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:08.943
-[groans]
-Pika, Pikachu!

00:01:09.027 --> 00:01:12.530
Raichu!

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:16.242
Unbelievable!

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:19.412
And I was always Ditto because
Ditto was one of my favorites.

00:01:19.454 --> 00:01:23.083
And a boy, one day, I was in 6th grade?

00:01:23.166 --> 00:01:25.960
Between 5th and 6th grade.
It was 6th in elementary.

00:01:26.044 --> 00:01:29.756
Because in 6th grade,
I became obsessed, just crazy

00:01:29.839 --> 00:01:31.674
for an anime called SHAMAN KING.

00:01:31.883 --> 00:01:33.551
Let’s go, Amidamaru!

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:34.677
Bason!

00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:35.970
Vorpal Dance!

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:36.262
Ainu

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:38.556
I watched it again recently and my heart--

00:01:38.681 --> 00:01:40.266
I love it. 

00:01:40.308 --> 00:01:42.894
Well, on my watch,
when there were no cell phones,

00:01:42.894 --> 00:01:46.856
I set it 15 minutes forward
and arrived 15 minutes before

00:01:46.898 --> 00:01:49.609
to watch the anime.
I was ready 30 minutes before

00:01:49.734 --> 00:01:53.029
in front of the TV, with my dinner served,

00:01:53.154 --> 00:01:56.533
to be able to see SHAMAN KING,
which lasted 20 minutes.

00:02:00.411 --> 00:02:04.833
About that, in Japan,
Otaku is a person much more obsessed.

00:02:04.916 --> 00:02:07.752
At least in Chile, and from
my understanding, in Latin America,

00:02:07.836 --> 00:02:12.132
we take the term,
but use it in a lighter way

00:02:12.257 --> 00:02:14.467
because we don't have another way to say,

00:02:14.551 --> 00:02:17.345
"Hey, I like anime, but calm down."

00:02:17.428 --> 00:02:21.057
We have no categories to say
how much you like anime.

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:23.226
So we said, "Oh, Otaku.

00:02:23.268 --> 00:02:25.478
You like anime? Oh, Otaku."

00:02:25.562 --> 00:02:29.315
There are people who say, "I'm not Otaku."
Well, that's fine. Each person decides.

00:02:34.362 --> 00:02:38.408
A tremendous media phenomenon occurred.

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:40.410
Let me tell you, at a national level,

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:43.163
which was called the "Urban Tribes".

00:02:43.204 --> 00:02:45.165
They began to form groups,

00:02:45.206 --> 00:02:48.501
So all the Tribes had a name.

00:02:48.585 --> 00:02:51.921
They had an essence, a look.
And you looked in a certain way.

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:53.006
Curiously,

00:02:53.089 --> 00:02:56.551
of the groups that I remember,
there were some like,

00:02:56.593 --> 00:03:00.930
Visual K, Oshare, Pecora, Lolita, Otaku,

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:03.516
and the most famous, the Pokemon.

00:03:03.641 --> 00:03:07.604
Of which only the Otakus,
they watched anime.

00:03:07.645 --> 00:03:11.566
I even remember
that one of the first things I saw,

00:03:11.649 --> 00:03:16.529
it was in the newspaper in Antofagasta,
a city that nobody knows.

00:03:16.613 --> 00:03:18.781
It was about the Lolitas.

00:03:18.865 --> 00:03:22.869
And it was so misinformed
that the Lolitas scared me.

00:03:22.952 --> 00:03:28.833
Because I thought they were obsessed women
with some dolls.

00:03:28.917 --> 00:03:31.461
And they thought the dolls were alive.

00:03:31.502 --> 00:03:34.297
And, indeed, because of that,
my mom was very scared

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:39.177
that I met these groups.
And I would say, "Mom, we watch anime!"

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:42.472
And there, I went
to the Anime Circles because

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:46.226
watching anime was illegal.
And, where could you watch anime?

00:03:46.309 --> 00:03:50.980
Thank you, Netflix, for making it legal.
But back then, there was no Netflix.

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:56.027
So my mom literally started going with me
to anime events.

00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:59.405
Later on, most of the Urban Tribes
disappeared.

00:03:59.489 --> 00:04:04.661
But the Otakus didn't disappear because,
unlike the rest of the Tribes,

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:06.496
ours is my Tribe.

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:10.375
It was a way of life.
We watched anime happily.

00:04:15.463 --> 00:04:19.467
This is a bit of a touchy subject.
I'm not going to go into so many details.

00:04:19.550 --> 00:04:22.053
But in Latin America,
maybe you already know,

00:04:22.136 --> 00:04:25.682
there are usually many social movements,
protests.

00:04:25.765 --> 00:04:29.769
And, in Chile,
a very big one happened last year.

00:04:29.852 --> 00:04:33.022
But what I do want to tell you is the part
about the people

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:35.483
in the massive protests that took place.

00:04:35.566 --> 00:04:41.656
The most significant part were the posters
which were related to anime.

00:04:41.739 --> 00:04:43.908
People were walking in the street
in Chile.

00:04:43.992 --> 00:04:48.037
Thirty-year-old guys, like me,
they walked with their NARUTO banners,

00:04:48.121 --> 00:04:50.581
banners from POKEMON, from YOYO,

00:04:50.665 --> 00:04:52.625
from SAILOR MOON.

00:04:52.667 --> 00:04:56.546
Actually, there are articles in English
related to the subject.

00:04:56.629 --> 00:04:59.924
Like, how Inosuke, KIMETSU NO YAIBA…

00:05:00.008 --> 00:05:00.049
(Seeing that you avoid fighting
for your country)

00:05:00.049 --> 00:05:02.260
The guy with the pig's head. That one.

00:05:02.343 --> 00:05:06.597
It was one of the icons
of Chile's revolution.

00:05:08.433 --> 00:05:11.853
There were people who went to the protests
in cosplay.

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:14.022
In Chile, there is a celebrity.

00:05:14.188 --> 00:05:18.693
There was a lady who got dressed
with a corporeal Pikachu.

00:05:18.735 --> 00:05:20.695
And she was dancing like Pikachu.

00:05:20.695 --> 00:05:22.822
And it went viral. Meme.

00:05:22.822 --> 00:05:24.240
Because the Pikachu fell

00:05:25.241 --> 00:05:28.328
and then the Pikachu got up.
And they all kept dancing.

00:05:28.328 --> 00:05:29.829
And she became Aunt Pikachu.

00:05:30.121 --> 00:05:34.083
And Aunt Pikachu was one of the icons
of the movement in Chile.

00:05:34.625 --> 00:05:37.337
And so, my dear friends, "Netflixistas."

00:05:37.337 --> 00:05:40.757
My thesis for "What's it like
being an Otaku in Chile" ends.

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:43.301
It's weird but powerful.

00:05:43.301 --> 00:05:45.011
Hit "like" to this video

00:05:45.094 --> 00:05:48.931
and comment about what it's like
to be Otaku in your country.

00:05:49.015 --> 00:05:49.223
Bye-bye.

00:05:49.223 --> 00:05:49.474
Bye-bye.

00:05:49.474 --> 00:05:50.516
Bye-bye.

